[38;2;124;124;124m$(a^2+b^2+1)^2 - (2b)^2 < 1$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$(a^2+b^2+1-2b)(a^2+b^2+1+2b) < 1$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$(a^2+(b-1)^2)(a^2+(b+1)^2) < 1$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the condition is $|w-i|^2 \cdot |w+i|^2 < 1$, i.e., $|w-i| \cdot |w+i| < 1$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mwhere $w = a+bi$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo we need: there exists a root $w = a+bi$ of $P$ such that $|w-i| \cdot |w+i| <[0m[38;2;124;124;124m1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow $|P(i)| < 1$. Let me use the factorization. Let $w_1, \ldots, w_n$ be the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mroots of $P$. Then $P(z) = \prod_{k=1}^n (z - w_k)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $|P(i)| = \prod_{k=1}^n |i - w_k| = \prod_{k=1}^n |w_k - i| < 1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince coefficients are real, roots come in conjugate pairs: if $w_k = a_k + b_k [0m[38;2;124;124;124mi$ is a root, so is $\overline{w_k} = a_k - b_k i$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $|P(i)| = \prod_{k=1}^n |w_k - i|$ and also $|P(-i)| = \prod_{k=1}^n |w_k + [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mi| = \prod_{k=1}^n |w_k - (-i)|$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBut since coefficients are real, $P(-i) = \overline{P(i)}$, so $|P(-i)| = |P(i)|[0m[38;2;124;124;124m< 1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore $\prod_{k=1}^n |w_k + i| < 1$ as well.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow multiply: $|P(i)| \cdot |P(-i)| = \prod_{k=1}^n |w_k - i| \cdot |w_k + i| = [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\prod_{k=1}^n |w_k - i| \cdot |w_k + i| < 1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $\prod_{k=1}^n (|w_k - i| \cdot |w_k + i|) < 1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf for every root $w_k$ we had $|w_k - i| \cdot |w_k + i| \geq 1$, then the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mproduct would be $\geq 1$, contradiction.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore there exists some root $w_k = a + bi$ with $|w_k - i| \cdot |w_k + i| [0m[38;2;124;124;124m< 1$, which is exactly $(a^2 + (b-1)^2)(a^2 + (b+1)^2) < 1$, i.e., [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$(a^2+b^2+1)^2 - 4b^2 < 1$, i.e., $(a^2+b^2+1)^2 < 4b^2 + 1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThat's the proof. Let me write it up cleanly.[0m

